{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>זחלתי</b> — I feared. And from it, <i>זוחלי עפר</i> (crawlers of dust), because people fear them, like the matter of fearsome things of old. Some say: <i>זחלתי</i> means 'I stepped back,' and so in the language of Kedar. And <i>זוחלי עפר</i> are so called because their manner of walking is the reverse of that of men."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:15.880187508Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}